 "HEIC (High Efficiency Image Container) is the format every iPhone has used by default since iOS 11 in 2017. It wraps HEVC-compressed image data — the same codec family as modern video — and delivers photos at roughly half the file size of a same-quality JPEG. Apple adopted it to save storage; the rest of the world hasn't fully caught up.": "heic-to-png,heic-to-webp",
 "That's the daily friction: HEIC attachments open wrong (or not at all) on many Windows machines, older Android devices, CMS platforms, ecommerce back-ends and printing services. If you've ever emailed a photo from an iPhone and been asked to resend it as a JPG, you've met the problem.": "heic-to-png,heic-to-webp",
 "ShiftRaw converts HEIC to PNG in your browser. The decoder is compiled to WebAssembly, works on any device — including the iPhone itself — and your photos are never uploaded.": "heic-to-png",
